Of course. Here is the content for your `.env.example` file, based on the variables shown in your image.

This file serves as a template for other developers, showing them which environment variables are needed to run the application without exposing your actual secret keys.

-----

### `.env.example`

```
# Flask secret key for session management and security.
# Generate one with: python -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(16))'
FLASK_SECRET_KEY="your_strong_secret_key_here"

# Google Gemini API key for question generation and grading.
# Obtain this from Google AI Studio.
GEMINI_API_KEY="your_gemini_api_key_here"

# --- Database Connection Details ---
# These are used to connect to your MySQL database.
MYSQL_USER="your_database_user"
MYSQL_PASSWORD="your_database_password"
MYSQL_HOST="localhost"
MYSQL_DB="your_database_name"
```